FOUR SYMBOLS SEAL — FUINJUTSU REFERENCE
Konohagakure Sealing Archive — Jonin+ / Sealing Corps

The Four Symbols Seal is a fuinjutsu that binds a target or chakra within
a four-point sealing array. It commonly works in concert with the Eight
Trigrams sealing style to regulate a jinchuriki's access to tailed-beast
chakra.

Application:
- Four anchor points define the sealing field; the array can strengthen
  or gate an existing seal.
- Used as a component of the Fourth Hokage's Nine-Tails seal to allow
  Naruto Uzumaki controlled access to a measure of the fox's chakra.
- Related large-scale variants (e.g., four-corner barrier arrays) are
  used defensively to enclose a target space.

Handling: Sealing arrays must be drawn precisely; an error in the array
can invert the seal's effect. Practice on inert objects before any live
application. Certified sealing personnel only.
